Package: unimlsurv
Type: Package
Title: Survival Analysis Modelling
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: person("Steve", "Shi", email = "19943405117@163.com", role =
        c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Steve Shi [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Steve Shi <19943405117@163.com>
Description: A time-to-event counterpart to 'uniml' with the same
        layering and the same objects. Survival outcomes are modelled
        with native engines ('survival' and 'rpart'), imputation,
        scaling, and encoding are fitted on the training data only,
        and the reported statistics are the ones the survival
        literature actually defines: Harrell's and Uno's concordance
        indices, the inverse-probability-of-censoring weighted Brier
        score of Graf and colleagues, the integrated Brier score, the
        cumulative/dynamic and Uno time-dependent areas under the ROC
        curve with their integrated versions, time-point calibration
        against Kaplan-Meier estimates with the integrated calibration
        index and related measures, stratified Kaplan-Meier plots with
        the log-rank test, and time-point decision-curve analysis. All
        time points are chosen by the user. Users of the 'mlr3'
        ecosystem can still register their own 'mlr3' survival learners
        through surv_register_learner().
